            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live web access, so I can’t verify today’s very latest headlines. As of my latest reliable information, NASA’s **Perseverance Mars rover** was still operating in **Jezero Crater**, studying rocks and sediments that may preserve evidence of Mars’ ancient watery environment.\n\nKey recent developments up to that point:\n\n- **Perseverance continued collecting rock-core samples** for possible return to Earth by a future Mars Sample Return mission.\n- It was exploring areas associated with an **ancient river delta and channel system** in Jezero Crater, including light-toned rocks of high scientific interest.\n- The rover’s companion helicopter, **Ingenuity**, ended its mission in early 2024 after rotor-blade damage, but it far exceeded expectations with dozens of flights.\n- NASA was also reassessing the **Mars Sample Return** plan because of cost and schedule concerns, while seeking lower-cost, faster options.\n\nFor the most current update, the best source is NASA’s Perseverance mission page or NASA/JPL news releases.",
